# Review ownership.
#
# CODEOWNERS on its own only *requests* a review. It becomes a merge requirement
# only if "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled in branch protection,
# which ADR 0001 keeps as an explicit owner action. This file is written so that
# turning that setting on later is safe rather than breaking.
#
# Cadence and what ownership means in practice are in CONTRIBUTING.md.

# Everything, unless a later line says otherwise. The last matching pattern wins.
*                                          @abdeslam-menacere

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The agent-gated data refresh, which ADR 0003 lets merge without a human.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These lines name a path and no owner, which clears ownership for those files.
# That is deliberate and it is the whole reason this file is not a single line.
#
# ADR 0003 permits a source-backed refresh confined to exactly these documents to
# reach `main` with no human approving it, after its agent reviewers and the
# deterministic gates have passed. Leaving them under the catch-all above would
# put a code-owner review request on every automated refresh pull request, and
# would block that merge outright the moment code-owner review became required —
# repealing a landed ADR through a file that never mentions it.
#
# The set is `ALLOWED_PATHS` in
# `.github/skills/modeltree-gates/scripts/gate-scope.mjs`, which is the gate that
# actually enforces the qualifying class. It is duplicated here because
# CODEOWNERS cannot import, so `web/tests/contributing/issue-forms.test.ts`
# parses that script and asserts the two sets are equal. Adding a document to the
# refresh's reach without clearing it here fails the suite.
#
# Everything else under `web/src/data/` — the schemas, the validator, the tests —
# stays owned by the catch-all above. A refresh cannot change them, so nothing
# here should.
/web/src/data/sources.json
/web/src/data/publishers.json
/web/src/data/organizations.json
/web/src/data/families.json
/web/src/data/releases.json
/web/src/data/benchmarks.json
/web/src/data/benchmark-results.json
/web/src/data/usage-observations.json
/web/src/data/usage-syntheses.json
/web/src/data/model-fit-statements.json
/web/src/data/model-fit-evidence-gaps.json
